Apple today seeded an updated version of the watchOS 27.2 release candidate, four days after the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/19/watchos-27-2-release-candidate/">first RC became available</a>.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/06/watchos-27.jpg" alt="" width="1319" height="742" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1051912" /><br/>
Registered developers and public beta testers can download software through the Apple Watch Settings app or using the Apple Watch app on iPhone.<br/>
<br/>
watchOS 27.2 adds new <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/siri/">Siri</a> AI features and extends &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; AI to more languages. <br/>
<blockquote>This update provides enhancements to Siri AI, including the ability to retain useful context from previous Siri interactions, draw from a wider range of personal context, and deliver faster responses on your watch. This update also includes other features, bug fixes, and security updates for your Apple Watch.<br/>
<br/>
- Siri AI can recall your past conversations, so you can ask Siri about something it told you before, like the restaurants it recommended last week<br/>
- Siri AI can draw from more sources to give you a great answer, including photos attached in Messages, Calendar event attendees, your voicemails, and better results from Safari history and Reading List from your phone<br/>
- Excluded Apps lets you choose which apps Siri, Search, and suggestions can access, all from one setting on your phone<br/>
- Siri AI now provides faster responses on Apple Watch<br/>
- Siri AI is available in more languages, with support for French, Japanese, Korean, Portuguese, and Spanish. Siri AI is not available in the EU or mainland China</blockquote>We are expecting watchOS 27.2 and the other 27.2 updates to launch next week. <br/>
